      "binding_and_reverse_mapping": "The seven trait variants and 17 weapon/mark/trait triplets agree across canonical config, UI receipt, map, and reverse weapon pages; image URL and item.icon path are distinct and match the image receipt.",
      "own_tiers_and_wrappers": "All seven own variants use damage_near .07/.08/.09/.10 per stack and 3.5 seconds; wrappers resolve to the exact parent/child templates. Base effective cap is five stacks with a shared timer refreshed by qualifying kills, including at cap. Held gates disable proc/stat while unwielded; timer continues; removing the source trait removes its children.",
      "trigger_and_timing": "A qualifying ranged close kill from the exact held item uses hit_world_position within 12.5m of the owner. Attack damage and died status resolve before the queued on_kill adds a layer, so the triggering hit is not retroactively changed. The hit-position trigger distance is separate from the damage consumer distance.",
      "benefit_formula": "The damage consumer uses attacker/target positions at Attack.execute time, interpolates damage_near to damage_far and ranged_damage_far with the clamped square-root curve from 12.5m to 30m, then contributes D-1 to the additive damage pool; it is not a universal final-damage multiplier. The documented 3-stack and 20m examples are numerically consistent under their stated neutral-modifier assumptions.",
      "attack_coverage": "The 17 actual marks’ direct ranged and special-hit routes align with the page. Direct special pellets can qualify; P1 Mk IX burning ticks and P4 Mk III stun ticks do not qualify; the P4 Mk VIII rending application has no periodic damage. Melee specials do not trigger, though their life-damage attack may read the active same-distance stat; the shield light bash is a pure push with no life damage.",
      "localization_and_ui": "The locale 0/16 names and description share the verified keys/hashes and RAW SHA. The four-tier reconstruction matches formatter output. The Chinese Close Damage wording is separately explained against the distance-based damage_near consumer. Shotgun P1 Mk VI is corrected to the actual UI spelling 紮羅娜.",
      "correction_delta": "The RAW reconstruction table’s static-rebuild note now sits in its own paragraph after a blank line; tier RAW strings and numbers are unchanged. Refreshed scope includes both corrected formal files and their synchronized canonical/resume proofs.",
      "verification": "All 63 current bytes match the frozen scope SHA map. Refreshed focused checks report 175 ranges/62 source files, zero new link errors, and GFM parsing of 24 tables/580 rows; no in-game behavior was claimed."
